On Mar 6, 11:31 am, Jym <Jean-Yves.Moyen+n...@ens-lyon.org> wrote:
> On Tue, 06 Mar 2007 20:24:20 +0100, <masquerade...@gmail.com> wrote:
> > I've heard mentions in many different places of intentionally avoiding
> > fights and decreasing your own level as a strategy. This is a newbie
> > question, but what is the advantage of limiting or decreasing your
> > level, what classes should do it, and when?

I think that there is a significant advantage to _not_ leveling up
fast.  With the exception of those hazards that are instakills to the
player with less than 20 or 30 hp and are essentially independent of
XL (e.g. Rolling boulder traps and the odd attack wand lying around)
there are advantages to not leveling up.  Specifically, monster
difficulty does not increase as fast.  5 or 10 or even 20 extra hp
means nothing when a mumak has your cornered.

One of the most critical components of survival does not increase with
XP, and that is AC.  You need to make sure that your equipment keeps
up with your XP.  HP can go away fast if your weapons or AC are
insufficient.  For a new player, I'd recommend keeping your pet with
you and keep your XL at 3 as far down as Sokoban and even into
Minetown.  I believe that the ability to level up in the early game is
too easy for one's own good and an early hazard.  I find that a good
way of keeping my character above the monster curve is by using my
pets to kill the guards in Minetown and doing the protection run at XP
= 1,2, or 3.

Basically, you'll find your own balance.  People ascend with many
different stles.  My advice is that if you over and over again
encounter monsters that are too much to handle, then you're probably
leveling up too fast.  Soldier ants and centaurs with wands of speed
monster are good tests; if they're too difficult then slow down.
However, once you're at Level 10 or 12 or so, you shouldn't need to
worry about it.  I learned how to survive soldier ants after being
able to do a pacifist protection run; but I learned how to ascend
after I learned to live without pets.

Good luck!
